# Never ship development configuration in a production image.
#
# The runtime image sets ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production, so these files are
# not *read* there — but they were still being copied in, which means the
# committed development JWT signing key and a LocalDB connection string were
# sitting in the published artefact of every image built. Anyone who can read
# the image layers can read the key, and the same key is the one a developer
# might paste into a real environment. A secret that ships is a secret that
# leaked, whether or not the process loads it.
#
# It also removes the failure mode where setting ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT to
# Development on a production container silently activates the committed key
# instead of failing to start.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.Development.json

# .gitignore classifies these as secrets and docker-compose steers developers
# into creating one at the repository root.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Backups, should an operator ever run the ops scripts with the repo as the
# backup directory. They would be large and they would be data.
*.bak
*.trn
